BenchmarkResponse.description:
Response model for benchmark operations.

Contains the full backtest results for the primary model (from backtest_config.forecaster)
plus a scores comparison dictionary for all comparison models, wrapped in a `data` field
for consistency with ForecastResponse and BacktestResponse (REQ-P2-4.2).

Attributes:
    operation_type: Discriminator field, always "benchmark"
    data: Dict containing "backtest" and "model_scores" keys. Empty {} when offloaded.
          - backtest: Dict mapping PRIMARY model name to its full backtest data
          - model_scores: Mapping of COMPARISON model name to scores dict
    session_id: Session identifier for result retrieval
    resource_id: Optional resource ID for large data offloading (set when data is offloaded)
    dataset_resource_id: Resource ID for the input dataset (e.g., "data:session_id")

Note on Offloading Consistency (REQ-P2-4.2):
    This structure matches ForecastResponse and BacktestResponse:
    - When data is inline: data={...}, resource_id=None
    - When data is offloaded: data={}, resource_id="response:session_id"
    Use _ensure_data_loaded() to transparently fetch offloaded data.

Example response (inline data):
    {
        "operation_type": "benchmark",
        "data": {
            "backtest": {
                "catboost": {
                    "predictions": [...],
                    "scores": {...},
                    "explain": {...}
                }
            },
            "model_scores": {
                "lgbm": {"mape": 0.12, "rmse": 0.45},
                "ridge": {"mape": 0.15, "rmse": 0.52}
            }
        },
        "session_id": "abc123",
        "resource_id": null
    }

Example response (offloaded data):
    {
        "operation_type": "benchmark",
        "data": {},
        "session_id": "abc123",
        "resource_id": "response:abc123"
    }

WorkflowErrorDetails.description:
Structured error information for a failed DBOS workflow.

Fields are partitioned by external visibility. New fields default to internal-only;
add to _EXTERNAL_FIELDS only when safe to expose to external consumers.
